Package: nutrigon
Title: Angular Separation Between Nutritional Optima
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Juliano", "Morimoto", email = "juliano.morimoto@abdn.ac.uk", role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-3561-1920"))
Description: Fits response surfaces (ordinary least squares, generalized
    linear models with any family including quasi-families, or linear
    mixed-effects models) to trait data collected under the Geometric
    Framework for Nutrition and computes the angular separation (theta)
    between the nutritional optima of two traits, with bootstrap confidence
    intervals. Provides local Gaussian and mean curvature and a surface-area
    ratio for a fitted surface, and a simulation-based per-result
    reliability diagnostic that compares a given result's risk-factor
    profile (curvature elongation, distance to the angular boundary of the
    design, and angular separation) against a pre-built validation grid of
    configurations with known ground-truth bootstrap coverage. Includes the
    Drosophila lifespan and fecundity dataset of Lee et al. (2008)
    "Lifespan and reproduction in Drosophila: new insights from nutritional
    geometry" <doi:10.1073/pnas.0710787105> as a worked example. Methods
    are described in Morimoto (2023) "Nutrigonometry I: using right-angle
    triangles to quantify nutritional trade-offs in performance landscapes"
    <doi:10.1086/723599>.
